WEBVTT

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:03.950 --> 00:05.650
Luchabull, Flying Press!

00:13.440 --> 00:14.100
Komoruu!

00:15.080 --> 00:16.330
Komoruu is unable to battle.

00:16.810 --> 00:17.630
Luchabull wins!

00:18.190 --> 00:19.170
That makes one victory!

00:22.460 --> 00:23.810
Komoruu, please return.

00:25.140 --> 00:26.670
I expected nothing less, Satoshi.

00:27.170 --> 00:28.540
But I will not lose this next one.

00:29.310 --> 00:31.040
Shota, do your best!

00:31.740 --> 00:37.260
As Satoshi and his friends continue their journey towards Eisetsu City, they reunite with Shota in a town.

00:38.010 --> 00:41.950
A three-on-three Pokémon battle then suddenly began.

00:43.040 --> 00:45.020
Please come out, Hitotsuki!

00:47.790 --> 00:49.300
Oh, a fresh face!

00:49.300 --> 00:50.280
So cool!

00:50.860 --> 00:52.420
You got a new Pokémon, huh?

00:55.540 --> 00:57.140
Hitotsuki, the Sword Pokémon.

00:57.730 --> 01:01.640
This Pokémon is said to be born when a departed spirit inhabits an ancient blade.

01:02.330 --> 01:04.050
All right. I'm counting on you, Pikachu!

01:05.610 --> 01:06.400
Let us begin!

01:06.690 --> 01:08.080
Fury Cutter!

01:12.260 --> 01:13.540
Iron Tail!

01:16.960 --> 01:18.390
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

01:25.200 --> 01:26.410
Ah, Hitotsuki!

01:28.170 --> 01:29.610
Hitotsuki is unable to battle!

01:30.160 --> 01:31.260
Pikachu wins!

01:31.640 --> 01:33.110
Pikachu is amazing!

01:34.120 --> 01:35.420
Well done, Pikachu.

01:37.550 --> 01:39.580
Hitotsuki, thanks for the hard work.

01:41.180 --> 01:43.620
It is disappointing, but this will give us EXP as well.

01:44.540 --> 01:46.000
My third is my ace.

01:46.570 --> 01:48.090
I will count on you, Jukain!

01:52.610 --> 01:53.850
So it has evolved.

01:54.330 --> 01:55.590
Then my third will be...

01:56.220 --> 01:58.330
Gekkouga, I choose you!

02:09.180 --> 02:14.900
The Strongest Mega Battle!
Gekkouga VS Mega Lizardon!!

02:16.160 --> 02:17.380
A Gekkouga!

02:18.030 --> 02:20.140
So <i>it</i> evolved too.

02:20.620 --> 02:21.520
Whoa!

02:23.930 --> 02:33.810
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:23.930 --> 02:33.810
Z

02:25.240 --> 02:28.520
Jukain, the Jungle Pokémon. The evolved form of Juptile.

02:29.150 --> 02:30.470
It has seeds growing on its back.

02:30.470 --> 02:33.670
They are bursting with nutrients that revitalize trees.

02:34.250 --> 02:36.330
Let us begin! Bullet Seed!

02:38.590 --> 02:39.590
Bring it on.

02:39.940 --> 02:40.720
Water Shuriken!

02:44.080 --> 02:44.800
Cut!

02:47.210 --> 02:48.240
Please evade it!

02:52.060 --> 02:54.250
As I thought, even though we have the type advantage,

02:54.700 --> 02:55.870
we must not take them lightly.

02:56.220 --> 02:57.320
It's not over yet.

02:57.320 --> 02:58.260
Aerial Ace!

02:59.780 --> 03:01.000
Leaf Blade!

03:17.360 --> 03:18.750
Dragon Pulse!

03:22.990 --> 03:23.420
Dodge!

03:32.160 --> 03:33.850
Can you keep going, Gekkouga?

03:34.750 --> 03:37.480
We will keep pressing them. Leaf Storm!

03:44.600 --> 03:45.190
Gekkouga!

03:45.920 --> 03:48.430
I have already analyzed Gekkouga's fighting style.

03:49.030 --> 03:52.910
It makes use of its speed to close in on its opponent, where it can instantly settle the match.

03:53.550 --> 03:56.750
That is why attacking from a distance is so effective against it.

03:57.200 --> 03:58.520
He's been studying them.

03:58.940 --> 04:01.380
Shota sees Satoshi as his goal,

04:01.790 --> 04:03.210
so it is only natural.

04:10.810 --> 04:13.240
Jukain, slam Gekkouga into the ground!

04:17.820 --> 04:20.020
Gekkouga, you can keep going, right?

04:20.020 --> 04:22.110
We'll win this match for sure!

04:43.000 --> 04:44.410
What is going on...?

04:45.130 --> 04:47.450
Jukain, let us focus and continue on!

04:49.920 --> 04:51.440
Let's go, Gekkouga!

04:54.120 --> 04:55.100
Aerial Ace!

05:08.870 --> 05:10.030
Jukain is unable to battle!

05:10.550 --> 05:11.600
Gekkouga wins!

05:11.990 --> 05:13.240
Therefore, the winner is Satoshi!

05:18.640 --> 05:19.790
Shota, I got this one.

05:21.290 --> 05:23.590
We are having a hard time catching up to Satoshi...

05:24.560 --> 05:27.300
But we have received some nice EXP.

05:27.850 --> 05:28.390
Satoshi!

05:28.970 --> 05:29.720
Are you all right?

05:30.260 --> 05:30.810
Yeah.

05:31.320 --> 05:32.190
But I'm tired.

05:33.020 --> 05:34.570
That was close, wasn't it, Gekkouga?

05:36.120 --> 05:41.230
Satoshi, what <i>was</i> that? How can you do that? Please tell me!

05:41.530 --> 05:43.460
I don't know either.

05:43.830 --> 05:46.610
My vision goes "bam" and then I'm all "rargh".

05:46.840 --> 05:47.740
I see, I see...

05:48.440 --> 05:50.510
Wait, that does not help!

05:53.140 --> 05:54.870
Everyone has recovered.

05:55.520 --> 05:56.920
Thank you very much.

06:00.810 --> 06:01.790
Welcome back, Pikachu.

06:03.840 --> 06:05.070
Over here!

06:05.070 --> 06:05.500
Yeah.

06:10.810 --> 06:13.390
Hello. Welcome to the Pokémon Center.

06:14.330 --> 06:15.460
Please heal it.

06:16.160 --> 06:16.540
Certainly.

06:24.810 --> 06:28.070
Satoshi, your Gekkouga's appearance changed a little, right?

06:28.070 --> 06:29.000
It did?

06:29.000 --> 06:29.920
Yes!

06:30.190 --> 06:32.070
Also, it was enveloped in water.

06:32.660 --> 06:35.070
What did you do to make that happen?

06:35.670 --> 06:36.330
Uh...

06:36.900 --> 06:38.970
I'm not really sure either...

06:40.740 --> 06:42.790
If only we knew...

06:42.790 --> 06:43.920
It happens without warning, right?

06:44.270 --> 06:47.080
The number of times it has happened so far can be counted on one hand too.

06:47.880 --> 06:49.050
That is strange...

06:49.660 --> 06:53.550
Your and Gekkouga's movements were perfectly matched.

06:54.120 --> 06:56.620
It was like that the other times it happened too, right?

06:56.840 --> 06:58.600
Hm... Let me think...

07:01.780 --> 07:03.590
I can't put it into words that well,

07:04.080 --> 07:11.020
but it almost feels like I experience whatever Gekkouga sees or does myself...

07:11.520 --> 07:11.960
Huh?

07:12.390 --> 07:15.070
Does that mean you fuse together?

07:15.540 --> 07:19.220
Then my mind and body flare up, like, "whoosh"...

07:19.580 --> 07:21.790
...and afterwards, I'm really exhausted.

07:22.150 --> 07:25.080
Does that mean you become Gekkouga, Satoshi?

07:25.080 --> 07:25.830
What?!

07:26.240 --> 07:28.160
Me? Become Gekkouga?

07:30.860 --> 07:33.130
If I could do that, that'd be cool I guess!

07:34.480 --> 07:36.260
What? I don't get what's going on.

07:36.790 --> 07:38.580
The brat turns into Gekkouga?

07:38.890 --> 07:40.400
No way.

07:42.580 --> 07:44.340
That is a bold hypothesis.

07:44.570 --> 07:46.030
That sounds fun!

07:46.030 --> 07:47.310
That'd be so like you, Satoshi.

07:47.850 --> 07:51.800
It is said that the deeper the relationship between a Trainer and a Pokémon gets, the more similar they become.

07:52.420 --> 07:58.280
This could certainly be a move you achieve <i>precisely</i> because of the deep bond with your Pokémon.

07:59.140 --> 08:00.060
Our bond makes...

08:01.180 --> 08:02.630
...me turn into Gekkouga...?

08:07.060 --> 08:07.450
Alan,

08:08.090 --> 08:13.910
as shown in the data I've just sent you, the Mega Evolution energy has been accumulating just fine.

08:14.220 --> 08:15.230
Thank you very much.

08:15.910 --> 08:16.280
Director?

08:16.910 --> 08:17.450
What is it?

08:18.430 --> 08:20.390
How are Manon and Harimaron doing?

08:29.840 --> 08:33.000
There's been no change. Neither in Manon nor in Harimaron.

08:33.310 --> 08:34.940
Understood. I'll hurry.

08:38.490 --> 08:39.430
I'll keep fighting...

08:40.510 --> 08:41.520
...until Harimaron wakes up....

08:41.800 --> 08:42.160
...and...

08:43.130 --> 08:45.790
...Manon smiles again.

08:52.630 --> 08:54.210
Satoshi, let us battle again!

08:54.650 --> 08:55.670
Yeah, sure!

08:56.000 --> 08:57.180
Do your best!

09:05.600 --> 09:06.420
Pokémon Quiz.

09:07.430 --> 09:07.940
The answer is...?

09:24.950 --> 09:25.790
All preparations are complete.

09:26.390 --> 09:27.880
Then let us begin.

09:28.300 --> 09:28.960
Understood.

09:30.960 --> 09:32.960
Be good, kids.

09:36.180 --> 09:37.620
The system is all clear.

09:38.120 --> 09:38.960
Recording has started.

09:39.770 --> 09:40.840
Begin with the experiment!

09:43.210 --> 09:44.250
Irradiating energy.

09:52.460 --> 09:55.260
We've confirmed a rise in Mega Evolution energy.

09:55.880 --> 09:59.110
Keep Z's metabolism at 50 percent.

09:59.400 --> 10:01.100
So far, everything is proceeding according to my calculations.

10:01.780 --> 10:03.320
Let's move on to the next stage.

10:03.880 --> 10:04.830
Converting the beam.

10:05.280 --> 10:07.100
Locking the range of the irradiation device!

10:11.700 --> 10:12.670
Now fire!

10:13.220 --> 10:13.710
Fire!

10:37.000 --> 10:39.880
To think a mere <i>ten</i> Cell can cause a response of this magnitude...

10:40.120 --> 10:41.990
Wonderful!

10:58.660 --> 10:59.210
Pikachu!

11:03.290 --> 11:05.130
Good morning!

11:05.600 --> 11:06.590
You guys are...!

11:06.970 --> 11:08.970
If you say "You guys are...!",

11:09.300 --> 11:11.240
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

11:11.770 --> 11:14.100
To prevent the world's destruction!

11:14.310 --> 11:16.310
To protect the world's peace!

11:16.870 --> 11:19.370
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

11:19.940 --> 11:22.160
we're lovely, charmy villains!

11:23.640 --> 11:24.280
Musashi!

11:24.780 --> 11:25.150
Kojiro!

11:25.610 --> 11:28.180
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

11:28.540 --> 11:31.110
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

11:31.480 --> 11:32.780
Just kidding!

11:37.000 --> 11:37.900
Blasted Rocket Gang!

11:38.510 --> 11:39.710
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

11:42.940 --> 11:45.990
Of course we have anti-electricity measures set up when we try to get Pikachu!

11:46.220 --> 11:48.070
The early bird catches the Pikachu!

11:49.370 --> 11:52.880
It took us until now to figure out this incredibly simple fact!

11:53.190 --> 11:55.230
When you're sleeping deep and sound,

11:55.230 --> 11:56.960
we can get it without effort!

11:56.960 --> 11:59.230
This is the super-simple early bird plan!

11:59.760 --> 12:00.590
We're going home!

12:02.560 --> 12:03.380
Pikachu!

12:06.620 --> 12:08.250
Wait for me, I'll go save you now!

12:10.830 --> 12:12.730
It's still early in the morning!

12:12.730 --> 12:13.880
Go back to bed!

12:14.330 --> 12:14.970
Pumpjin!

12:15.190 --> 12:15.790
Maaiika!

12:18.410 --> 12:19.040
Satoshi!

12:19.710 --> 12:20.720
Psybeam!

12:20.720 --> 12:21.750
Shadow Ball!

12:29.730 --> 12:30.970
Are you guys all right?

12:31.340 --> 12:31.720
Yeah!

12:32.120 --> 12:32.900
We're fine!

12:32.900 --> 12:33.880
Satoshi, behind you!

12:34.780 --> 12:36.280
Pumpjin, Dark Pulse!

12:50.320 --> 12:51.570
What?!

12:54.500 --> 12:55.400
A Lizardon?

12:56.490 --> 12:59.070
Who are you?! This is none of your business, you creep!

12:59.580 --> 13:01.830
Stop sticking your nose in <i>our</i> affairs!

13:02.200 --> 13:04.060
Lizardon, Dragon Claw!

13:07.680 --> 13:08.260
What?!

13:10.720 --> 13:12.090
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

13:18.320 --> 13:20.020
Lizardon, bring Pikachu to safety!

13:23.680 --> 13:25.390
And it was going so well, too!

13:25.770 --> 13:28.320
I really liked that early bird plan...

13:28.700 --> 13:30.970
So what's the deal with that Lizardon?

13:33.190 --> 13:35.370
This feels bad!

13:40.750 --> 13:41.420
Pikachu!

13:42.920 --> 13:44.120
Well done, Lizardon.

13:46.490 --> 13:47.930
Satoshi, are you all right?

13:48.300 --> 13:48.810
Yeah.

13:49.420 --> 13:50.170
Excuse me...

13:50.580 --> 13:54.890
That was quite a feat, firing a Thunderbolt mid-air in that posture.

13:55.430 --> 13:58.490
But it couldn't have done that if it hadn't been for the Lizardon...

13:59.140 --> 14:00.640
Thank you, Lizardon.

14:05.180 --> 14:06.590
Is that a Mega Stone?

14:06.990 --> 14:08.070
I had no idea Lizardon could also...

14:08.580 --> 14:09.290
Wanna see?

14:10.090 --> 14:12.820
Let's have my Lizardon and your Gekkouga battle.

14:13.270 --> 14:13.510
Huh?

14:14.500 --> 14:15.750
I saw your battle yesterday.

14:16.520 --> 14:17.580
I wanna see that again.

14:18.060 --> 14:18.710
Understood.

14:19.350 --> 14:19.960
Let's do this!

14:27.380 --> 14:28.960
Let's go, Lizardon!

14:32.610 --> 14:34.130
Gekkouga, I choose you!

14:37.050 --> 14:39.120
He said that he watched yesterday's battle, so...

14:39.510 --> 14:41.470
Yeah, I think he saw when Gekkouga did that thing.

14:43.280 --> 14:44.940
I will serve as the referee.

14:45.590 --> 14:47.920
This will be a single-round match where you will use one Pokémon each.

14:48.490 --> 14:50.540
If one of them is unable to battle, they lose.

14:50.810 --> 14:51.370
Is that all right?

14:52.380 --> 14:52.810
Yeah.

14:53.030 --> 14:53.660
Now then,

14:53.930 --> 14:54.280
begin!

15:02.780 --> 15:03.720
We'll start.

15:04.080 --> 15:04.790
Water Shuriken!

15:08.310 --> 15:09.200
Dragon Claw!

15:13.920 --> 15:14.760
It cut straight through it!

15:14.960 --> 15:15.940
Is that even possible?

15:18.090 --> 15:19.760
That's not all there is, right?

15:19.760 --> 15:21.400
Gekkouga, Cut!

15:23.270 --> 15:23.680
Dodge!

15:28.070 --> 15:28.610
Flamethrower!

15:38.190 --> 15:39.400
Come on, show me.

15:39.880 --> 15:40.280
Let's go!

15:40.920 --> 15:42.160
Respond to my heart,

15:42.500 --> 15:43.220
Key Stone!

15:44.940 --> 15:46.120
Surpass evolution!

15:46.630 --> 15:47.600
Mega evolve!

16:14.500 --> 16:16.110
I knew it'd mega evolve!

16:17.540 --> 16:18.880
A black Lizardon...

16:18.880 --> 16:20.070
Awesome, awesome, awesome!

16:20.930 --> 16:23.620
I have never seen one before. It radiates power...

16:24.200 --> 16:25.680
This has become even more exciting!

16:26.190 --> 16:27.950
Let's make sure to win, Gekkouga!

16:29.040 --> 16:30.140
Let's go, Lizardon!

16:31.520 --> 16:32.300
Dragon Claw!

16:35.380 --> 16:36.070
Cut!

16:41.120 --> 16:41.870
Double Team!

16:42.310 --> 16:42.850
Flamethrower!

16:51.460 --> 16:52.430
Aerial Ace!

16:54.320 --> 16:55.400
Thunder Punch!

16:59.550 --> 17:00.110
An Electric move!

17:01.940 --> 17:02.590
Gekkouga!

17:06.720 --> 17:08.910
Come on, show it to me already!

17:09.270 --> 17:10.640
Thunder Punch, once more!

17:12.250 --> 17:13.040
Water Shuriken!

17:21.850 --> 17:22.560
Gekkouga!

17:27.390 --> 17:29.040
Gekkouga, are you all right?

17:30.720 --> 17:32.850
Let's show it to them all right! Show them our power!

17:55.380 --> 17:57.460
So it mega evolves without the use of a stone, huh...?

17:58.180 --> 17:59.960
Is that a testament to their bond?

18:01.120 --> 18:02.080
Aerial Ace!

18:05.370 --> 18:06.470
Fly up, Lizardon!

18:12.000 --> 18:12.910
Thunder Punch!

18:13.300 --> 18:14.150
Cut!

18:28.000 --> 18:29.030
Blast Burn!

18:42.220 --> 18:43.590
Gekkouga is unable to battle!

18:43.940 --> 18:45.300
Therefore, Lizardon wins!

18:49.050 --> 18:50.430
It's so strong...

18:54.300 --> 18:55.210
That was excellent.

18:59.540 --> 19:01.110
Gekkouga, are you all right?

19:03.240 --> 19:04.440
Yeah, I am too.

19:05.270 --> 19:06.320
Can we please do this again some time?

19:06.750 --> 19:07.120
Sure.

19:07.990 --> 19:09.350
We'll work harder...

19:09.980 --> 19:11.510
...and become stronger, you'll see.

19:11.820 --> 19:13.040
Right, Gekkouga?

19:16.860 --> 19:18.280
My name is Satoshi.

19:18.680 --> 19:19.540
And you...?

19:20.900 --> 19:21.800
I'm Alan.

19:22.550 --> 19:23.470
Alan-san, is it?

19:24.070 --> 19:24.820
Just Alan is fine.

19:25.370 --> 19:25.660
Okay.

19:32.890 --> 19:33.990
That Gekkouga...

19:34.570 --> 19:36.080
I wonder what we need to do for it to transform.

19:38.230 --> 19:39.610
Let us do an analysis.

19:39.990 --> 19:41.770
I think science could help us find something out.

19:42.720 --> 19:44.860
Really? I'm counting on you, Citron!

19:46.200 --> 19:47.280
Satoshi and Alan...

19:48.160 --> 19:52.380
At that point, nobody knew that their encounter would mark...

19:52.970 --> 19:55.790
...the beginning of the greatest crisis to befall Kalos.

20:01.140 --> 20:04.650
Fleur-de-lis-sama, the experiment was a success.

20:15.920 --> 20:20.880
Sunday February 7th at 8am!

20:16.700 --> 20:20.440
Let'Z Peh!! In fiercely burning battles

20:17.200 --> 20:19.870
Popular comedians gather at Pokénchi!

20:23.750 --> 20:25.620
PokéLove TV!

20:26.130 --> 20:30.480
All right, here comes PokéLove TV, which spreads the charm of Pokémon to the world!

20:30.480 --> 20:31.720
The hosts are I, Ken, and...

20:31.720 --> 20:33.830
Hi! I'm Jenny, nice to meet you!

20:33.830 --> 20:37.120
Today we will introduce Mega Lizardon X!

20:37.120 --> 20:40.430
What's up with that Lizardon? It's so fancy, wearing a choker like that!

20:40.430 --> 20:44.430
That's called a Mega Stone. It's indispensable for Mega Evolution.

20:44.430 --> 20:50.430
Also, when it mega evolves, Mega Lizardon X changes its appearance and becomes a Dragon type!

20:50.430 --> 20:51.520
No way!

20:51.840 --> 20:53.300
Mega evolution is awesome!

20:53.300 --> 20:54.600
All right, I've decided!

20:54.600 --> 20:56.130
Huh? What?

20:56.130 --> 20:58.340
I'll also mega evolve and increase my girl power!

20:59.150 --> 21:02.180
Oh, but you can't mega evolve.

21:02.670 --> 21:06.850
Lots of other Pokémon have been discovered to mega evolve, so here, check them out!

21:07.610 --> 21:10.730
Whoa, there are so many! I wonder if they'll discover my Mega Stone as well!

21:11.400 --> 21:14.880
I told you; you can't mega evolve!

21:18.110 --> 21:20.020
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.210 --> 21:21.300
Towards our next adventure!

21:21.940 --> 21:23.970
All right, let's get Squishy!

21:23.970 --> 21:25.550
If we do that, Sakaki-sama...

21:25.550 --> 21:26.630
...will be delighted as well!

21:26.630 --> 21:27.470
Uh, hey, look at that!

21:27.470 --> 21:28.510
It's Squishy!

21:28.510 --> 21:29.940
We're so lucky!

21:29.940 --> 21:31.460
But... isn't the color a little different?

21:31.460 --> 21:33.890
There's one more like Squishy?!

21:33.890 --> 21:35.030
That really...

21:35.270 --> 21:36.980
...feels good!

21:37.220 --> 21:39.960
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:39.960 --> 21:42.420
The Explosive Land's Wrath! Operation: Capture Zygarde!!

21:42.440 --> 21:45.880
Next Time

21:42.440 --> 21:45.880
The Explosive Land's Wrath!
Operation: Capture Zygarde!!

21:42.810 --> 21:44.760
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:45.930 --> 21:55.980
Next episode:

21:45.930 --> 21:50.900
Kojiro gets Zygarde!?

21:46.760 --> 21:51.360
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

21:50.930 --> 21:55.980
Clash! The Rocket Gang VS the Flare Gang!!
